I'm a terrible Nethack player.  I've never gotten to the quest.  A good
game for me is one where I make it to Minetown or the Oracle.  I descend
too fast, I don't take the time to carefully identify items, and thus I
have short and awful games.

So tonight it was a bit of a shock when I got my first Named Demon
kill.  I'd been playing an Orc Barbarian, and had found an altar on DL3
or so.  So I'd been sacrificing stuff on it, and had sacced a couple of
goblins and hobgoblins, and, *boom*, there's Juiblex.  Which was OK--he
was peaceful and not doing much to bother me.

So I hung around a while longer, killing and sacrificing, and then a
light exploded and I went blind.  Well, while blind, something hit me,
and I hit back at where I thought it was, and, well, whacked Juiblex.
At this point I was only 7th level.

He engulfed me.

So I started whaling on him from the inside, and it didn't take many
hits at all before I killed him.  Sure, at that point I was very sick,
but I was able to pray and was cured.  (Not that it ultimately helped; I
eventually guessed the timing wrong, got hungry, hadn't had my prayer
timeout met, pissed off my god, and got beaten to death by a dwarf
because I fainted while trying to kill him.)

So, uh, is Juiblex SUPPOSED to be that much of a wuss when you hit him
from inside his own guts, or did I get very very lucky?

